title: 'answer-window nudge TTS failures are syslog-only: broad except means no payload or transcript signal'
updated_at: "2026-08-23T08:06:52Z"
---
Stated plainly by the B187/B177 agent as a known gap it deliberately did not widen scope to fix.

src/hark/answer_window/open_window.py:458 and :538 wrap the spoken-nudge run_tts in a broad `except Exception`, so a nudge TTS failure never propagates.

It is NOT fully silent - each logs speech.no_open_nudge_failed / speech.empty_stt_nudge_failed at level="warn" with the error string. The gap is that a failed nudge appears in syslog ONLY: not in the ask/listen JSON payload, and not in transcripts.jsonl.

Why it matters: the nudge is how Hark recovers a stalled answer window ("I did not hear anything - are you there?"). If the nudge itself fails to speak, the operator hears nothing at all and the turn just times out, while every surface an agent reads reports a normal timeout rather than "the recovery prompt could not be spoken". That is a misdiagnosis waiting to happen.

Related and worth doing together: B187 fixed WHICH provider the nudge speaks through (it was using policy.stt_provider). This is about whether anyone finds out when it fails.

Fix direction: narrow the except to the provider-error class, and surface the nudge outcome in the window result so it reaches the payload. Do not simply let it raise - a failed nudge must not abort a window that is otherwise fine.

Documented as a known gap in docs/PROVIDERS.md under the "A downgrade is never silent" section - keep the doc and the fix in sync when this lands.